claimed: deploy-doctor-cli -- stage 0's second half (specs/deployment.md):
the clean-machine doctor and the `okay deploy` CLI over deployment.json.

Tool/Manager/Presence with a NotReady probe (installed and still unusable
is the common case, not the rare one), a Tools catalogue, Doctor.check
producing the table and the same fields as --json, and opt-in --install
that prints each command before running it and never pipes from the
network. Then Cli: render/doctor/up/down/diff/targets reading the
rendered deployment.json rather than evaluating Scala, with the exit
codes the spec names (3 = a prerequisite is missing) and every shelled
failure carrying its command line, code and last output.

Files: okay-deploy/src/main/scala/okay/deploy/{Doctor,Tools,Cli,Shell}.scala,
okay-deploy/bin/okay, okay-deploy tests, specs/deployment.md, boards.
